---
import PageLayout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import siteConfig from '~/config/site';

const updated = 'This template has not been dated yet.';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy"
  heading="Privacy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  intro="What this site collects, which is close to nothing."
  description={`How ${siteConfig.name} handles visitor data.`}
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]}
>
  <section class="wrap sec" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="prose rev">
      <p class="form-note">
        <strong>Template — replace before you publish.</strong> This page is a starting
        point written for the demo site, not legal advice. Edit it in
        <code>src/pages/privacy.astro</code> to describe what your deployment actually
        does, and have it reviewed if your jurisdiction requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>What this site collects</h2>
      <p>
        As shipped, this theme is a static site. Fonts are served from this domain.
        Project inquiries go through LinkedIn rather than a contact form on this site.
        No analytics cookies are set by the site itself.
      </p>

      <h2>Server logs</h2>
      <p>
        Whoever hosts the site will keep standard access logs — IP address, user agent,
        requested URL and timestamp. Those are the host's records, kept under the host's
        retention policy. Name your host here and link to their privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
      <p>
        There is no contact form on this site. If you message through LinkedIn, that
        platform processes the conversation under its own terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Anything you add</h2>
      <p>
        Analytics, embedded video, a comment system, a newsletter widget or a chat bubble
        each introduce their own data collection. If you add one, describe it here.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about any of this can go through
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/alexia-bejarano-52b412152" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="mini muted">{updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
